\page char Character

Everything displayed on the terminal is whether an ASCII or an UTF-8 character.
To encompass all the possible characters, a type named `nocterm_char_t` with 4 byte buffer is created for the Nocterm project.

This type is one of the building blocks of the **buffers** of **widgets** alongside with `nocterm_attribute_t`.

---

There are various functions to create Nocterm compatible characters and strings

- `nocterm_char_from_ascii()` can turn a character literal to `nocterm_char_t`.
- `nocterm_char_from_wchar()` can turn a unicode character literal to `nocterm_char_t`.

Below example shows the aforementioned character functions in action:

```c
#include <nocterm/nocterm.h>
 
int main(){
 
    setlocale(LC_ALL, "en_US.UTF-8");

    nocterm_char_t my_ascii_char = nocterm_char_from_ascii('A');
    nocterm_char_t my_utf8_char = nocterm_char_from_wchar(L'Ğ');

    nocterm_io_put_char(my_ascii_char);
    nocterm_io_put_char(my_utf8_char);
    
    return 0;
}
```

It is also possible to convert a C string to a `nocterm_char_t` based string, or vice versa.

```c
#include <nocterm/nocterm.h>
 
int main(){
 
    nocterm_char_t my_string[10] = {0};
    
    nocterm_char_string_from_stream(my_string, 10, "hello", 6);

    for(int i = 0; i < 10; i++){
        nocterm_io_put_char(my_string[i]);
    }

    return 0;
}

```